Principal UX/UI audit (#123, docs/design/audits/ux-ui-principal-audit.md, ADR-0013). Behaviour that CSS and the Arabic
overlay cannot change:
- UX-01: a saved chat opens on its newest message (upstream default: the first one); the setting still turns it off.
- UX-04: the chat footer is translated (com_efaiw_chat_footer) whenever CUSTOM_FOOTER is set, so the English interface no
  longer shows the Arabic trust notice; the variable stays the switch that replaces upstream's text.
- UX-06: the sign-in page says what it does (title and button), and with password reset off it tells the user to contact
  the administrator instead of offering nothing.
- UX-07: a language switch on the sign-in page (the same three steps as the settings selector).
- UX-08: Arabic dates are numeric dd/mm/yyyy: «21 أكتوبر 2026» did not fit the files panel.

